 # C3: Per-agent read cursor — persistence + advance-on-handle
-# C3: Per-agent read cursor — persistence + advance-on-handle
-
-THIS CHUNK IS THE BUG FIX for TAT-68. Per-agent cursor in a SQLite cursors table (agentId × roomId → last_seq), NOT Pi appendEntry/session files (the thing we're escaping). Advance the cursor on agent-turn completion (last-delivered → cursor), not a specific tool call, so silent/non-tool turns still advance correctly. Advance-on-success semantics: delivered-but-uncommitted messages re-deliver on resume (correct); committed messages never re-deliver (kills the bug). Abort/resume is safe by construction. Legacy cursor initialization: start at current HEAD, not beginning — replaying full history as unread would dump the whole log into context, the opposite of the goal. Depends on C1 (TAT-71) for the log table and C2 (TAT-72) for audience data.
+# C3: Per-agent read cursor (Tattler layer) — persistence + advance-on-handle
